{"skill":{"slug":"agent-browser-core","displayName":"Agent Browser Core"},"version":{"version":"1.0.1","createdAt":1770369553491,"changelog":"- Added comprehensive safety guidelines in a new `agent-browser-safety.md` reference file.\n- Updated orientation and documentation links to include safety and high-risk operation controls.\n- Introduced \"Safe mode defaults\" section to the main documentation, outlining recommended restrictions for secure automation.\n- Revised supporting references to clarify safe usage practices.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":2049,"sha256":"58451246bf423fcf7959e444708029f87df011318be3ffad588933efa3edea6c","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/agent-browser-workflows.md","size":875,"sha256":"5d4cabfe21369a289b9b6e44565139a79b1c66d314bab8724a99d35c16413deb","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/agent-browser-troubleshooting.md","size":549,"sha256":"953ba49d147125d7be7f21430d0bb145c6da631b57d72507f9e6eba91be84dd8","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/agent-browser-overview.md","size":1226,"sha256":"147e3add2caa2f90268d2f4b6ebf34d748e8cfbd39bcecb9dabab1d1b61dd499","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/agent-browser-safety.md","size":1009,"sha256":"ffe1934872ef50fd6847d8d7e7e80b461925a018e502b4b10ac8b9ebad0bec35","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/agent-browser-command-map.md","size":1148,"sha256":"11b43415c27514b15bcc9c377f272825c1b7ab32e09a4d6ff5b02c70a59ed293","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2476,"sha256":"216089161b73ef2abe597913b337759a8e3674648648d30928ce816dbdb1ea47","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789036570263,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"e7aed139b9420b055b70db88e9d019a367dfe53fe5063db8c277a1d1a4476b75","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/e7aed139b9420b055b70db88e9d019a367dfe53fe5063db8c277a1d1a4476b75","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: agent-browser-core\nVersion: 1.0.1\n\nThe skill bundle consists entirely of documentation and metadata for an 'agent-browser' CLI tool. All markdown files (SKILL.md and references/*.md) consistently emphasize security best practices, explicitly warn against high-risk capabilities like `eval`, `--allow-file-access`, and network manipulation, and instruct the AI agent to prioritize safe mode defaults and human approval for sensitive actions. There is no evidence of malicious intent, data exfiltration, unauthorized execution, or prompt injection attempts to subvert the agent; instead, the instructions guide the agent towards secure and controlled operation.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779161814881},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":8,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":1,"checkedAt":1789036570263},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a coherent browser-automation documentation skill with disclosed high-risk controls, though users should pin and isolate its install commands.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Browser automation can access authenticated sites and browser state, but the skill advises allowlisting domains, blocking private networks, using dedicated environments, avoiding elevated privileges, and redacting secrets.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The install guidance includes dynamic package/runtime installation, including global npm installation, agent-browser browser downloads, and an unpinned npx Playwright fallback; this is disclosed and purpose-aligned but should be pinned and isolated by users.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"High-risk actions such as eval, file access, credential/state handling, traffic manipulation, proxies, custom browser arguments, and downloads are identified as sensitive and tied to explicit approval or task necessity.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The referenced CLI uses a background daemon and supports saved state/profile reuse, but the artifacts disclose this, recommend ephemeral sessions by default, and treat state files as sensitive.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill is a Markdown playbook for the agent-browser CLI, and the documented capabilities match web automation via snapshots, refs, sessions, and structured commands.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only in a dedicated non-root environment, pin exact trusted versions of agent-browser and Playwright, avoid global installs where possible, and require explicit approval before using file access, eval, credential/state mutation, proxies, or traffic interception.","findings":"[RP1] expected: The unpinned npx Playwright install-deps example is a legitimate supply-chain caveat, but it appears in installation documentation for a browser automation tool, is not hidden or automatic, and is surrounded by guidance to pin versions, isolate installs, and avoid elevated privileges.\n[T08] expected: The dynamic browser/runtime installation commands are expected for this CLI workflow. They should be treated cautiously, but the artifacts do not show malicious packages, remote payload execution by the skill itself, deception, or automatic execution.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789036570263}}}}}